From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:28:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/27] sycl : register-fed DPAS for XMX q4_K/q6_K decode
 matmuls

GGML_SYCL_XMX_Q4K_DIRECT / GGML_SYCL_XMX_Q6K_DIRECT (default off): each
lane builds its weight row's s8 operand in registers from the reorder
layout and feeds DPAS via intel_sub_group_i8_i8_matrix_mad_k32
(cl_intel_subgroup_matrix_multiply_accumulate), skipping SLM staging.
Same math and order as the joint_matrix kernel (bit-identical at equal
split-K), 7-12% faster per op on Arc B70, 1..8 columns. Built as a
separate libggml-sycl-xmxd.so because the device-linked main library
cannot resolve the builtin. _DIRECT_CHECK=1 memcmps against the old path.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
